@comment{
  Bibliography for "Casino Royale: FIVE 00s — Special-Agent Mission Software".
  Ingested by the Pandoc --citeproc render.

  Every key below is cited at least once from a numbered manuscript section,
  and every `[@key]` in those sections resolves to a key below. That is not a
  convention, it is a gate:
  tests/test_manuscript_variables.py::TestBibliography fails in either
  direction. Under --citeproc a bibliography with no in-text citations emits
  nothing at all, so an uncited entry is a silently dead reference — this file
  used to carry one (a self-citation of the manuscript itself, since removed;
  the package's own citation metadata lives in CITATION.cff).
}

